From: iLinux workspace
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: app-nap=on|off|auto display option

A hidden QEMU window lets macOS App Nap the process: all threads, vCPUs
included, drop to background priority (PRI 4) on efficiency cores, so a
guest busy with user work runs ~5x slower (measured: 3.5 vs ~21 Gop/s).
app-nap=auto holds NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep while
non-background vCPUs are busy (>25% of a core over 1 s) and releases it
after 10 idle seconds, so an idle hidden guest still naps.  off = never nap.
Default stays "on" (upstream behaviour).

diff -ru a/qapi/ui.json b/qapi/ui.json
--- a/qapi/ui.json	2026-10-12 01:22:56
+++ b/qapi/ui.json	2026-10-12 01:22:56
@@ -1459,6 +1459,12 @@
 # @zoom-interpolation: Apply interpolation to smooth output when
 #     zoom-to-fit is enabled.  Defaults to "off".  (Since 9.0)
 #
+# @app-nap: macOS App Nap policy.  "on" lets macOS nap QEMU whenever
+#     its window is not visible, which runs the whole guest at
+#     background priority on efficiency cores; "off" never naps while
+#     the VM runs; "auto" naps only while the guest's non-background
+#     vCPUs are idle.  (default: on)
+#
 # Since: 7.0
